## Chief Information Security Officer
Location:
London
Team:
Corporate Functions
Employment Type:
Regular
Job Code:
A225078
Share this listing:
Responsibilities
Team Introduction
The Global Payment team of ByteDance provides payment solutions - including payment acquisitions, disbursements, transaction monitoring, payment method management, foreign exchange conversion, accounting, reconciliations, and so on to ensure that our users have a smooth and secure payment experience on ByteDance platforms including TikTok.
Responsibilities:
- Own IT service management and operations for systems supporting e-money issuance, payment services, safeguarding, customer servicing, finance, and regulatory reporting;
- Implement and maintain IT governance, risk, and control frameworks proportionate to the business, covering infrastructure, access, change, backup/recovery, monitoring, and vulnerability remediation; support risk assessments, control attestations, and governance reporting for senior management and committees;
- Partner with Information Security and business stakeholders to embed security controls across IAM, privileged access, endpoints, logging, patching, encryption, and backup protection;
- lead operational resilience, BCP, and DR arrangements, including asset mapping, failover testing, single-point-of-failure identification, and remediation;
- Oversee change management and systems delivery, ensuring all IT changes are assessed, approved, tested, and documented; manage outsourcing and third-party technology arrangements, monitoring service performance, security, control reports, concentration risk, and contractual obligations for critical providers;
- Serve as the key IT operational contact for audits, regulatory reviews, and major incident escalation; coordinate evidence collection, regulatory reporting, and senior management reporting on IT performance and risks; set objectives and performance standards for managed service partners and ensure adequate staffing, skills coverage, and training.
This role will be based onsite at our office and will require a 5-day onsite work arrangement.
Qualifications
Minimum Qualification(s):
- Bachelor's degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Information Security, Engineering, or a related discipline (or equivalent professional experience);
- 5+ years of relevant experience in IT operations, infrastructure, service management, or technology risk & control roles;
- Experience in a regulated financial services firm — preferably an EMI, payment institution, bank, fintech, or other FCA-regulated environment;
- Experience supporting governance forums, management reporting, and cross-functional remediation programmes;
- Proficient in both English and Chinese to facilitate effective communication and collaboration with Chinese-speaking stakeholders across the business.
Preferred Qualification(s):
- Relevant certifications such as ITIL, ISO 27001, COBIT, CISSP, CISM, CRISC, or cloud platform certifications are preferred.

# Senior Analyst - Technology Team - London
London, United Kingdom
(On-site)
## Job Description
Lazard is one of the world’s leading financial advisory and asset management firms. **Our people make the difference**. With just over 3,000 employees, our tight-knit community allows for professionals eager to learn and willing to teach to connect and grow together. We believe that diversity, equity, inclusion, and allyship are not just business imperatives — they are central pillars of our employee experience. Our entrepreneurial culture and flat structure allow creative ideas and original concepts to drive our business forward — and for careers to take flight.
Through our financial advisory business, Lazard advises clients around the world on strategic and financial matters including mergers and acquisitions, restructurings, capital structure and capital raising. Our client relationships are built on trust and discretion. As the world’s largest advisory-focused firm, we have exceptional depth of expertise across industry sectors and geographies. We value the rich diversity that comes from blending local perspective with our global network.
**Senior Analyst – Technology M&A Team – London**
Lazard is seeking to recruit a Senior Analyst to join the Technology Team in London.
Lazard is seeking to recruit a Senior Analyst to join the Technology Team in London. As one of Europe's leading independent Technology team[s], Lazard has advised on many of the most high-profile transactions in the sector over the past decade. The team is regularly engaged with key industry players including both corporate clients and financial sponsors across the full spectrum of Tech verticals.
We are looking for a proactive, enthusiastic and motivated individual, with at least 2 years M&A experience, to join the team in London.
**We’ll trust you to:**
* Demonstrate strong technical and analytical skills with an ability to build financial models with ease;
* Research, analyse, sensitise and adapt both internal and client-facing financial and statistical analysis/ models;
* Efficiently evaluate qualitative and quantitative data;
* Be responsible for the accuracy of numerical work produced by junior bankers before delivering the final product to senior bankers;
* Be responsible for assisting in the preparation and production of presentations and marketing materials for clients and prospective clients, in consultation with other team members;
* Effectively manage their own work and that of juniors, taking responsibility for accuracy and quality-checking finished products with regards to content, consistency and language
* Assist MDs and senior bankers on an ad hoc basis as needed with various reports and analyses;
* Handle execution and process matters flawlessly, assisting in due diligence efforts as appropriate;
* Understand client objectives and recommend potential solutions;
* Show an ability to identify ideas for the creation of new business;
* Use your own knowledge and judgement to add information to presentations where appropriate;
* Identify issues arising and offer potential solutions. Create productive relationships with clients and advisors;
* Communicate effectively and appropriately;
* Turn ideas into concise and comprehensive presentations;
* Be a proactive team participant with a natural ability to develop their profile across Lazard groups and regions;
* Anticipate needs and be proactive in making value-added contributions;
* Independently develop sound and logical views whilst understanding both the big picture and the minutiae;
* Show confidence, professionalism and accountability at all times;
* Contribute to firm-wide initiatives including recruiting, training and professional development.
**You’ll need to have:**
* Gained relevant M&A experience within an investment banking environment. Previous M&A transaction experience would be helpful but is not essential;
* Robust understanding of the accounting principles that underlie typical financial analyses used in advisory (particularly valuation);
* Outstanding financial understanding that can be readily translated into modelling that is used for both marketing and execution purposes;
* Self-motivation, with demonstrable ability to manage conflicting priorities and requests in a high pressure environment;
* The ability to take initiative and function independently, balanced with strong team skills;
* Excellent interpersonal and relationship-building skills, with the ability to maintain relationships with colleagues and clients at all levels;
* Strong verbal and written communication skills;
* The ability to deliver requested materials to senior bankers in a timely manner;
* Strong awareness of the regulatory environment;
* The skills to maintain high standards of professional and ethical conduct, adhere to legal and regulatory requirements of the banking environment and follow Lazard policies and procedures;
* Minimum 2.1 university degree classification (or equivalent if studied outside the UK);
**What we offer**
We strive to enhance the total health and well-being of our employees through comprehensive, competitive benefits. Our goal is to offer a highly individualized employee experience that enables you to balance your commitments to career, family, and community. When you work for Lazard, you are working for an organization that cares about your unique talents and passions, and will continue to invest in the development of your career.
**Does this sound like you?**
Apply! We’ll get in touch on the next steps.
**Representation at Lazard**
Lazard is an intellectual capital business committed to delivering the best advice and solutions to clients. To achieve these objectives, we focus on attracting, developing and retaining the best talent. We believe that a workforce comprised of people who represent a wide array of backgrounds, experiences and perspectives creates a rich variety of thought that empowers us to challenge conventional wisdom, solve problems creatively and make better decisions.
Lazard was built on the premise that a multicultural firm can best serve a global clientele. As a global firm that has grown organically from local roots in different countries, we have a deep tradition of respecting and appreciating individual differences. Doing so has been core to our success for over 175 years. We are committed to sustaining an environment where every colleague is supported in their professional pursuits, can maximize their individual potential and contribute to our collective success.

## Project Manager (VM / Retail Fit-Out)
PARDGROUP SPA LONDON, United Kingdom Project Management Hybrid
### Company Description
Pardgroup, a leading company in integrated services for retail and large-scale distribution, is looking for 2 new **Project Managers** to join our UK team in London.
### Position
Reporting to the Head of Projects, the Project Manager will work closely with the production and delivery teams and will carry out the following activities:
* End-to-end project ownership across assigned client portfolios, including project delivery, account management, and stakeholder coordination;
* Coordination and supervision of Visual Merchandising, window display, pop-up, rollout, and retail fit-out projects;
* Management of the entire workflow, from client briefing and planning through to installation and final delivery;
* Coordination of suppliers, subcontractors, and internal teams to ensure projects are delivered on time, within budget, and to the required quality standards;
* Preparation of project costings, quotations, and support in developing client proposals;
* Monitoring project progress against deadlines, budgets, and quality requirements, proactively resolving issues where required;
* Support in evaluating suppliers, materials, and production solutions;
* Management of multiple projects simultaneously, often at different stages of delivery;
* Ensuring compliance with health & safety requirements, including RAMS (Risk Assessments and Method Statements).
### Requirements
You will have:
* 3-5 years of previous experience in a Project Management role within luxury retail, Visual Merchandising, retail fit-out, or related environments;
* Proven experience managing window displays, pop-ups, retail activations, retail rollouts, or store fit-out projects;
* The ability to manage multiple projects, clients, suppliers, and stakeholders simultaneously;
* Strong organisational, communication, and client management skills;
* Knowledge of IT software and programmes, including Excel, MS365, and ideally AutoCAD;
* Commercial awareness with strong problem-solving and decision-making abilities;
* A collaborative approach with excellent interpersonal skills;
* Experience working in fast-paced retail environments and managing high volumes of projects.
### Other information
Nice to have:
* ·A background in architecture or technical design would be advantageous.
* ·Fluency in Italian would be a plus.
*Pardgroup is an equal opportunity employer.*

# Aquatic Ecologist | Expression Of Interest
## Cambridge, GBR
**Join our** **Freshwater** **Aquatic** **Ecology** **Team**
We are growing our Freshwater Aquatic Ecology team and are looking to connect with talented aquatic ecologists who are passionate about protecting, enhancing and restoring freshwater environments across the UK and Ireland.
We welcome expressions of interest from aquatic ecologists across all grades, from Consultant through to Senior Principal. Whether you are looking to develop your technical expertise or seeking an opportunity to help shape the future direction of a growing team, we would love to hear from you.
You will work on nationally significant and technically challenging projects, collaborate with a supportive and multidisciplinary team, and help clients deliver sustainable development while protecting and enhancing the freshwater environment.
As our team continues to grow organically, there are opportunities to influence technical capability, mentoring, service development and the delivery of projects across the UK and Ireland. We are committed to creating an environment where people are supported to grow, develop technical specialisms and pursue their own professional interests whilst contributing to the success of the wider team.
We are proud of the collaborative and supportive culture we have built, where knowledge sharing, teamwork and professional development are valued alongside technical excellence.
Working alongside regional and national technical leaders, you will play a key role in delivering freshwater aquatic ecology expertise across a diverse portfolio of projects, supporting clients from the earliest stages of planning and survey design through to environmental assessment, project delivery and long-term monitoring.
**We are actively interested in speaking with candidates across multiple grades and locations throughout the UK and Ireland and recognise that** **great talent** **can come from any location**
**What** **You’ll** **Be Working On**
Our team supports a varied portfolio of work across the water, energy, infrastructure and development sectors, including:
* Strategic water resource and drought resilience schemes;
* Nationally significant infrastructure projects;
* River restoration and nature recovery initiatives;
* Fisheries and fish passage assessments;
* Water Framework Directive (WFD) assessments;
* Freshwater ecological monitoring programmes;
* Hydropower and renewable energy developments; and
* Ecological and environmental impact assessments.
No two projects are the same. Your work will directly contribute to understanding, protecting, enhancing and restoring rivers, lakes, reservoirs, canals and other freshwater habitats.
You will also have opportunities to collaborate with specialists across ecology, hydrology, hydrogeology, geomorphology, hydraulic modelling, environmental planning and engineering, providing integrated solutions to complex environmental challenges.
**About You**
We are looking for passionate aquatic ecology professionals with consultancy, regulatory, academic or industry experience.
**You’ll** **have:**
* A degree in Aquatic Ecology, Ecology, Environmental Science, Fisheries Science or a related discipline;
* Membership of a relevant professional body (e.g. CIEEM, IFM or CIWEM), with chartered status desirable for more senior roles, or a willingness to work towards professional accreditation;
* Experience undertaking, managing or interpreting freshwater ecological surveys and assessments;
* Knowledge of relevant environmental legislation, planning policy and regulatory frameworks applicable to the jurisdictions in which you work;
* Experience in one or more areas of freshwater ecology, which may include:
* Fish, macrophyte, macroinvertebrate or diatom surveys and assessments;
* Fish passage and barrier assessments;
* Aquatic habitat surveys and assessments (e.g. habitat walkovers, RHS, RCA and MoRPh);
* Hydroecology and environmental flows;
* River restoration and nature-based solutions;
* Ecological and Environmental Impact Assessment, including EcIA, EIA and Environmental Statement inputs;
* Habitats Regulations Assessment (HRA) or equivalent; or
* WFD assessment and compliance;
* The ability to undertake technical reporting and communicate scientific information clearly and accurately;
* Strong written and verbal communication skills; and
* The ability to contribute to project delivery, client relationships and technical guidance at a level appropriate to your experience.
**For Principal and Senior Principal grades, we would also welcome experience in:**
* Providing technical leadership and mentoring;
* Designing and managing freshwater survey and monitoring programmes;
* Managing projects, programmes, budgets and multidisciplinary workstreams;
* Developing and maintaining strong client and regulatory relationships;
* Supporting business development and preparing technical and commercial proposals;
* Undertaking technical review and quality assurance;
* Leading complex environmental assessments; and
* Supporting the growth and development of technical services and team capability.
**If your experience does not tick every box, we still encourage you to apply. We hire people, not checklists**
**Particular Areas** **of Interest**
While we are keen to hear from aquatic ecologists with a broad range of skills and experience, we are particularly interested in candidates with expertise in one or both of the following areas:
* **Macrophyte survey,** **assessment** **and reporting** , including macrophyte identification, application of WFD survey methodologies, and interpretation of LEAFPACS outputs for ecological classification and assessment; and
* **Aquatic ecological data analysis using R** , including data management, statistical analysis, data visualisation, reproducible workflows and the interpretation of freshwater ecological datasets.
Experience in either of these areas is not essential for all roles. We welcome expressions of interest from candidates with strengths across the wider aquatic ecology discipline.
**Why Join Us**
* We put people first: We're proud of our friendly, inclusive and collaborative environment where everyone feels valued and driven to succeed.
* We are driven to achieve: Named in the top 50 companies to work by Glassdoor 2025. Recognised by Corporate Knights as one of the world's top 10 most sustainable companies in 2025. Named 'Best Place to Work' and 'International Consulting Firm of the Year' at the NCE Awards 2024.
* We do what is right: Industry-leading training and development, as well as paid professional subscriptions. A professional progression plan, supporting you to become chartered.
* We are better together: A supportive and collaborative team environment and Early Careers peer group, and a wider ERG network (see more on our ERGs here: Stantec Employee Resource Groups)
* Growth: We're on an exciting growth journey across the UK - we want you to be part of it!
* Great Benefits: Competitive salary, bonus schemes, enhanced pension plan, annual leave with the option to buy/sell additional days, private medical insurance, group income protection & life assurance included as standard, as well as discounted gym membership and lots more.
* Hybrid / Flexible working: Enjoy a healthy work-life balance with our hybrid approach.
